# factory2 — one factory, two products, two recipes competing for shared stock
# same two suppliers as factory1, but now the factory knows TWO recipes, each its
# own pathway. pick one in the dropdown to make only that product; choose "all
# edges" and BOTH recipes run at once, drawing on the same A and B — they compete.
# competition is the usual ground truth: nothing makes one product in isolation.
#
# widget is a lean 1:1 recipe. gadget is greedier — it needs 2 A per unit — so
# when both run they pull A down together and the scarce supplier throttles the
# pair. change the k's or the coefficients and the product mix shifts.
node supplyA : range(0, 50), init(0) @ bucket(fill = water)   # raw material: fluid
node supplyB : range(0, 50), init(0) @ bucket(fill = water)
node widget  : range(0, 50), init(0) @ box(fill = squares)    # finished units: a crate
node gadget  : range(0, 50), init(0) @ box(fill = squares)

external sourceA
external sourceB

sourceA -> supplyA : constant(c = 1)
sourceB -> supplyB : constant(c = 3)

# two recipes drawing on the same A and B:
pathway make_widget : supplyA + supplyB -> widget : limiting(k = 0.5)
pathway make_gadget : 2 supplyA + supplyB -> gadget : limiting(k = 0.5)
